-- CK-296: R-5.3.7, #955 (blocks O4a): a fold whose accumulator has an
-- unnamed cyclic type (`List (List (List …))`, checker-v2.md §7.3) checks
-- clean with no limit. `n` writes nothing; `m`, the twin, folds with
-- `List.push`, which edits the item `List.foldr` hands it, and keeps its two
-- accepted lines. Red: each round of v1's callback fixpoint adds one `[*]`
-- step that nothing folds, so both declarations print `limit …: fixpoint,
-- unsettled after 32` (`ownership_limit` under enforcement). The golden
-- claims the verdict lines and the totals.
n : Int
n = List.length (List.foldr [] [] List.intersperse)


m : Int
m = List.length (List.foldr [] [] List.push)
